  "pivot_note": "ONE pivot for all 28 frames, the centre of the drawn ellipse. A per-frame pivot makes the field hop; the fireball's impact set shares one value for the same reason.",
  "palette": {
    "colours": 47,
    "note": "all 28 frames were quantized TOGETHER in a single reduce_colors call at 48 colours, so they share one palette. Quantizing frame by frame is the mistake that tool exists to prevent."
  },
  "byte_warning": "selected_sha256 is the sha256 of THESE files. Copy them verbatim; never re-encode, re-crop or round-trip.",
  "ground_decal_note": "this is a FLAT GROUND decal, not a billboard. 128x72 is 1.78:1, the isometric foreshortening of a circle under the committed camera Euler(30,-45,0); the committed ca_sigil_floor_mark is 2.09x1.19.",
  "playback": {
    "form": {
      "frames": "form_0..8",
      "order": "0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8",
      "loop": false,
      "note": "the field settling in after the cast. One-way."
    },
    "hold_loop": {
      "frames": "hold_0..8",
      "order": "0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,7,6,5,4,3,2,1",
      "loop": true,
      "note": "PING-PONG, and this is required. Played 0..8 straight the wrap is 1.19x the largest interior step and the field visibly hitches every cycle. Ping-pong is seamless by construction. Measured: consecutive-frame mean diff avg 3.2, wrap 7.5. Dropping leading frames makes it WORSE (ratios 1.79-2.50) because frame 0 is an endpoint of a one-way drift, not an outlier."
    },
    "expire": {
      "frames": "expire_0..8",
      "order": "0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8",
      "loop": false,
      "note": "THE SPRITES DO NOT VANISH AND ARE NOT MEANT TO. They show the frost losing its structure - crystals shrink away, rim needles retreat - ending as a flat pale patch still covering 43.6% of the canvas. The DISAPPEARANCE is an alpha fade the engine applies over these frames. Binding them without a fade leaves a pale patch on the floor forever, which reads as a bug."
    }
  },
  "art_direction": {
    "hue": "pale cyan-white, explicitly NO green and NO teal. NSC-088 requires the spectral phantom to read clearly distinct from the Lantern Wraith's teal wisp, so frost must not crowd that hue. Art Director's pick, 2026-09-23.",
    "not_reviewed_in_engine": "nobody has seen these in Unity. They have never been imported and no human has approved them."
  },
